# Install HELM

| curl -fsSL -o get_helm.sh https://raw.githubusercontent.com/helm/helm/main/scripts/get-helm-4
chmod 700 get_helm.sh
./get_helm.sh |

| helm create helm-name | create a helm chart |

# go to templates folder and delete the default templates. Cretae your own templates

go back to your helm folder

| helm install release-name . | deploys all the products from the templates |

| helm ls | gives the release ionfo | we can use this info to rollback |

| helm upgrade release-name . | updates the changes made in the templates |

| helm uninstall release-name |

| helm package helm-name/ | create a tgz file to p[ush to github to help share the helm-charts, like we share docker images through docker hub |

| helm repo index . | creates index.yml file |

# We need botgh index and the gunzip file to push to github 

# once the files are ready push them to github and create a github page for the repo

# to downoad the helm repo from the github page to your new cluster

| helm repo add myrepo https://killadi98.github.io/helm-demo/ |

| helm repo ls | list of repos |

| helm repo update | to update any chnages from the original repo |

| helm install release-name myrepo/helm-name | to deploy the objects from the helm |

# we can use the same helm charrt to deploy the application in a ny cluster or any name-space

| helm install release-name myrepo/helm-name -n dev | to deploy the objects from the helm in the dev namespace |






